WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.690
A full moon at winter's end.

2
00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:07.560
A bonfire blazes; grain and
coconuts go into the flames.

3
00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:10.880
Next day, the streets explode with colour.

4
00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:15.200
Old and young, rich and poor,
throw powder at each other.

5
00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:20.090
Months later, in autumn, Bengal
fills with temporary shrines.

6
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.670
Inside, a warrior goddess is
welcomed with lamps and prayer.

7
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.390
On the last day, her clay
image goes to a river.

8
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:34.160
So why bonfires and colours, and why
welcome a warrior goddess home each autumn?

9
00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:38.200
In this mission, you'll uncover
the stories behind each festival.

10
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:41.010
Then you'll follow Durga Puja day by day,

11
00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:43.680
and see how communities keep it alive.

12
00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:48.770
Your mission: find out what Holi and Durga
Puja mean to the Hindus who keep them.
